{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree near-identical walkers discover a ticket's replacement link (iterate `deps` for `duplicates`, then `find_inbound_relationships` for `supersedes`): `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:58-108` (`_has_live_replacement_link`), `close_precheck.py:111-151` (`_recorded_replacement_target`), `src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py:76-118` (`find_replacement`), wrapped again by `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:166`. They differ only in liveness check and return type. Bug `frolicky-dependable-peccary` came from `verdict()` consulting only `find_replacement` while the \"not_a_bug needs no link\" rule lived in a comment in `_ensure_duplicate_close_is_linked` (`close_precheck.py:169-174`); the `DISPOSITION_CLASSES == _NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` equality is held only by a test (`close_disposition.py:43`).\n\n## Approach\nOne `close_disposition.replacement_of(ticket_id, tracker, *, require_live: bool) -> str | None`; `_has_live_replacement_link` and `_recorded_replacement_target` become one-line wrappers kept as monkeypatch seams (the 738a tests patch the boolean). `_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` imports `DISPOSITION_CLASSES` so the equality is structural. Guard: the `duplicates`/`supersedes` walk (`find_inbound_relationships(` combined with `\"supersedes\"`) appears only in `close_disposition.py`.\n\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py`.\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: a duplicate with a live target closes; edge: a duplicate whose target is itself closed-as-duplicate is refused; not_a_bug needs no link. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_close_disposition_attestation_738a.py`, `tests/unit/test_close_gate_disposition_69b9.py`, `tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One walker body remains; checked by the guard test and `grep -c \"supersedes\" src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` equal to 0.\n- [ ] Pinning suites pass with no assertion edits; checked by `pytest` and `git diff --stat`.\n- [ ] `_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` is defined as an import of `DISPOSITION_CLASSES`; checked by reading `txn.py`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787354973085791001,"uuid":"aa8be136-8e2e-4596-8a2d-f0941518c1cf"}